    <briefdescription>
<para>Mathematical domain error. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classcslt_1_1DomainError" kindref="compound">DomainError</ref> represents an error when an input value is outside the valid domain for a mathematical function (e.g., negative input to square root, log of negative number).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example Usage:</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>DomainError();<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>&quot;Math<sp/>domain<sp/>error&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>DomainError(&quot;Cannot<sp/>compute<sp/>sqrt<sp/>of<sp/>negative<sp/>number:<sp/>-4&quot;);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
